Russian =D1=88/=D0=B6 are typically pronounced as retroflexes /=CA=82/=CA=
=90/, whereas English
uses /=CA=83/=CA=92/. In Lojban the nonretroflex sound seems to be primary,=
 although
the retroflex version is acceptable.

stevo

